values ('f4a5b6c7-8d9e-4f34-9b34-4c5d6e7f8a34', 'theater-history-ii', 'Theater History II', 'This course surveys theater and performance from the 19th century to the present, tracking realism, modernism, political theater, postwar experimentation, American drama, global and diasporic theater, devised and documentary practices, and contemporary digital and institutional change. Students study plays, manifestos, reviews, production records, video documentation, and theater institutions while asking how modern theater history is shaped by power, preservation, labor, technology, race, gender, sexuality, disability, empire, and audience culture.');

